<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! Field Collision ~ where the house's models meet the outside record

Each slot states what the outside field rules for the house's three models — identity-as-relation, no-global-now, carriage-not-registry — tagged VINDICATE · CONTRADICT · EXTEND · GRAVE. The collision that found each finding, with its sources, quotes and measurements, reads in the research record <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/field-collision`>> under the same slot name; the rulings it rests on read at #/rulings.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/strongest-ground`>>

!! The strongest ground ~ the ontology the field reaches twice

''SPKI/SDSI (RFC 2693) and KERI converge independently on the house's ontology'' (VINDICATE): names read locally, authority rides a rolling key-state rather than a registry, succession grafts the key-state, the identifier stays fixed while its holders change, and duplicity gets caught without a clock. The field arrives at this model whenever it takes decentralization seriously. The caution holds beside it: SDSI lost the market to X.509's global CAs, so the better naming theory does not win on merit.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-coniks-resolution`>>

!! Equivocation-detection takes the form of carriage

''Carriage-not-registry keeps equivocation-detection.'' CONIKS catches a lying authority by gossiping a compact signed commitment (the Signed Tree Root) compared per reader, never by publishing the directory; KERI catches duplicity through watchers that gossip what they saw. A compact commitment, announced by its authority, replicated causally and compared as of each reader's view satisfies carriage term for term, so the registry filter holds whole (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/registry-filter`>>).

''Watchers stand owed.'' A per-reader view catches equivocation only when readers compare views. The house holds the duplicity-proof primitive (a veto out-competes as proof-of-contradiction, no clock); the watcher layer that circulates head-sightings stands unbuilt. A watcher gossips a signed "the head I saw for prefix X" — a sighting announced by its observer, so carriage, never a compiled who-is-who.

''The watcher's home splits in two layers'' (#/rulings): the ''Herm'' (the near-open crossroads relay, `carry⊥read`, sealed bytes — <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/dreamnet-architecture`>>) carries sighting-gossip blind and never watches; the ''Meshpalace'' (the Scope-1 CID/CAD/CRDT DreamNet gossip sensorium, ITC/`getHeads`-shaped; `convergent-mesh` #three-clocks, `corpus` #organ) holds the watcher: it gossips a signed head-sighting, compares incoming sightings against its own view and the chain, and surfaces two inconsistent heads for one prefix as a duplicity proof the veto/fold consumes (`identity-classes#the-two-forks`).

''Readiness, as the code stands:'' the mesh-palace flow-map stands (`mesh-palace.ts`: dial-records, cap-stacks, route slots) and serves as the map, carrying no head-sightings, no view-comparison and no duplicity surface. The Meshpalace sensorium does not stand in code (no `meshpalace_io`, no gossip router). The ITC primitive (`itc.ts`), `detectDuplicity` (`wax-stamp.ts`) and the veto/`foldPersonaContests` stand, and consume a duplicity once two inconsistent events sit in a chain. Watchers await a whole palace, not a wire.

''The field's blueprints:'' did:webvh pairs ledger-free pre-rotation (`nextKeyHashes`, the twin of `nextHandleKeyDigest`) with an in-protocol witness+watcher layer, its watchers named on the published document — so a handle card that names the watchers that sighted a head hands a reader a starting set to compare. KERI supplies the role vocabulary: Watcher, Juror, Jury, Judge, under "first seen, always seen, never unseen." Willow, Iroh, Veilid, DXOS and UCAN push equivocation-detection up to the application, so no local-first substrate supplies the owed watcher; the field's under-provision confirms the layer bears load.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/golden-principles`>>

!! Golden principles the field converges on ~ hold these

* ''No-global-now holds as a hardware law'' (FLP · CAP · PACELC). The house takes weakened liveness (φ-accrual) and says so. PACELC names the tax at peace: the house stands PA/EL and ''never offers a linearizable read''; every gate says so.
* ''Fork/join membership without a roster stands proven in theory'' — Interval Tree Clocks: fork yields two clones with disjoint event ids, join merges them, event increments locally, no central authority. The quorum-rollover rests on that mechanism. No deployment claim stands for ITC; the vindication rests on the mechanism alone.
* ''Weak subjectivity names the boundary'': a node offline past a horizon cannot self-heal from cryptography alone and needs an out-of-band social checkpoint — beyond horizon K a lone island asks a human — and social consensus MUST NOT carry more than that.
* ''Data-protection-by-architecture'' (GDPR Art. 25): pseudonymization by default, minimal extent, period and accessibility. The rejection law reads as a compliance posture, not only an aesthetic.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/anti-patterns`>>

!! Anti-patterns ~ measured graves, do not dig them

* ''Frozen identity'' (Secure Scuttlebutt): identity bound to one keypair with no rotation. The house escapes it by construction — the name binds a rolling quorum (the k-of-n HandleGlamour), with the rolling recovery commitment and armed inception as pre-rotation.
* ''Silence stays ambiguous'' (TUF freshness): a withheld update and a slow link look identical, so hardening-by-silence MUST bound its wait, and silence across K local epochs counts only while those epochs advance.
* ''Sybil rings blend into the social graph'': no reader distinguishes a k-of-n Handle from a self-vouching ring; the cost-dial (rb>c, the voucher co-pays) prices sybil and never eliminates it.
* ''Registry thinking drags back the confused deputy'' (Miller): any residual place that enumerates holders acts as an ACL. Carriage-not-registry stands as the security-correct choice.
* ''Target-unbound signatures'' (the Bluesky did:plc hijack: malleable id + shared genesis + no target-binding): `handleEventBytes` binds `prefix`/`handleKeyDid`/`ownerSetHash`/… into the signed bytes with explicit keys, so a signature never replays onto another head, key, set-epoch, owner or fork, and `handlePrefixOf` yields a full, fixed-length, domain-tagged sha256. No signed surface may let two byte-strings canonicalize to one identifier.
* ''Delegation without revocation'' (NIP-26): a delegation verb ships only beside its burn.
* ''Revocation that rests on cache freshness'' (UCAN): capability revocation (kapae/antigen) needs the watcher gossiping the contradiction.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/pattern-integrities`>>

!! Pattern-integrities ~ the waves, not the water

* ''Local names over global identifiers'' — human-meaningful naming rides as a local overlay on a machine-meaningful identifier; fusing them yields phishing or unmemorable keys. The Handle-over-edge rides this wave.
* ''Improper names'' (Deseriis) — a ''multiple-use name'' (Luther Blissett; the Dread Pirate Roberts) maps onto the 1-of-1-that-many-present Handle; a ''collective pseudonym'' (Wu Ming; a chartered cabal) maps onto the k-of-n-chartered Handle.
* ''Duplicity-detection stands as the deep dual of registry'' — a lying authority gets caught by detecting equivocation (two signed statements that cannot both hold), never by consulting a registry of truth. The veto out-competes causally because it carries proof-of-contradiction. The watcher layer (#the-coniks-resolution) supplies the water this wave needs.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-mesh-field`>>

!! The federated-mesh field ~ what the deployed systems rule for the identity design

* ''KERI vindicates the handle-KEL'': acceptance by TOAD (N≥2F+1) matches the leased-projection compare-and-swap; pre-rotation (commit the digest of the next key-set) belongs in the rotate/burn verb family and defends against a dead attacker only — a live capture of current+next keys falls to recovery-quorum (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/live-equivocation`>>).
* ''did:plc vindicates the authoritative-log + thin-local-index split'' and names its own residual centralization: order and time. A clockless ordering ambient makes the central directory unnecessary.
* ''CONIKS vindicates the read-side fork-catch'': per-reader audit of a compact commitment, no global monitor (#the-coniks-resolution).
* ''The Θ-model and the time-free failure detector vindicate clockless standing on a ratio'': liveness reads against the ratio of message delays, never an absolute bound — the ambient yardstick.
* ''Graves avoided by construction'': SSB's frozen identity; Farcaster's single global IdRegistry (the registry the filter forbids); did:key's unrotatable self-certifying names (the KEL indirection reads necessary); SSB fusion-identity's shared secret — so a Nexus or quorum key MUST take the form of a group key (FROST · KERI multisig), never a shared secret.
* ''Extensions the field proves missing'': Lifeguard's local health multiplier, logarithmic suspicion decay over independent corroborations, and buddy-first refutation; FROST (RFC 9591) signing k-of-n as one key while a KERI group AID keeps rotation visible — the veil tier picks which; Willow range-based set reconciliation for forked-head catch; and the law that correctness resolves on content or digest, never a self-asserted time.
* ''The sharpest insight'': the field decentralizes order and time last. The carriage-liveness ambient replaces, for the mesh, the one primitive everyone else still cheats on; if it fails, every rung silently re-grows a global now.
* ''Co-stimulation answers moderation'': never sever a realm or a human on one suspicion — require K independent corroborations plus a damage signal, the same instrument as the ambient's corroboration.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/standing-tensions`>>

!! Standing tensions ~ what the field leaves open (operator-aware)

* ''Moderation at scale.'' Hidden human-cardinality removes "ban the person, not the account." A ban propagates by capability (kapae/antigen, the vouch-lineage slash), never by de-anonymizing; a k-of-n name a ban cannot reach one human behind stands as a cost accepted for the pre-SIN stance.
* ''Beneficial-ownership law'' (US CTA · EU AMLD) — doctrine (#/rulings): the sovereign carriage never holds a KYC record; the legal record lives entirely at the web2 bridge (`bridge-and-reach-plane`), behind a causal-island boundary, with foreign credentials as `#has` caps held apart. A Handle that undergoes KYC crosses into a contract plane outside the sovereign wall and leaks no holder into carriage. The contract-plane KYC artifact stands unbuilt (a declared red).
* ''The live-equivocator exposure'': detection and recovery each sit in the other's blind spot; the Θ-ratio and Lifeguard's starved-observer back-off mitigate the coupling and do not close it. Its law, the field's answers and what a ruling waits for read at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/live-equivocation`>>.
* ''The clockless-verdict fork: READ FREE, ACT BY CONTRACT'' (#/rulings). Clockless accrual rides a monotone quantity driven by parties other than the neglected one, which the ambient supplies; a real-time bound R binds only where a consequence hurts a party, and lives in the parties' own bilateral contract, never a mesh-wide law. The ahi kā reading stays a log-fact plus attenuation, clockless, accusing nobody; `readAhiKa` performs exactly that reading. `ambientFloor 8 · warmRatio 0.30 · coldRatio 0.05` serve as fiction-QA defaults until the infrastructure stands to iterate around them; a verdict off them reads as good-enough-to-act-on, never a measurement.
* ''The credible-exit tax lands only on the sealed plane.'' At family scale (2-10 vessels) refusing an aggregator costs about nothing; at civic scale discovery, search, freshness and cold-start cost real work. Handle cards stand public by design, and a reconstructible, non-authoritative index of public handle cards counts as carriage, which the filter permits; no index stands over the sealed read-set. Any card-index stays a pointer readers verify against the KEL themselves, never a source of truth.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/rulings`>>

!! Rulings

# Operator ruling 2026-09-08: the watcher's home splits in two — the Herm carries sighting-gossip blind, the Meshpalace sensorium watches (#the-coniks-resolution).
# Doctrine firmed 2026-09-08: beneficial-ownership records separate at the island wall and live at the web2 bridge, never in sovereign carriage (#standing-tensions).
# Operator ruling 2026-09-11: the clockless-verdict fork reads free and acts by contract (#standing-tensions).
# Operator ruling 2026-09-13: `ambientFloor 8 · warmRatio 0.30 · coldRatio 0.05` stand ratified as fiction-QA defaults (#standing-tensions); the same day set the live-equivocation pull-forward lean aside (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/live-equivocation#/rulings`>>).
